       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose or formulation**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional."
